@* An info mark under a host that closes on Escape, which is the only
   arrangement that can see where the key stops.

   The live shape is the dashboard takeover: the shell's workspace surface carries
   a keydown handler that closes the surface on any Escape that reaches it, and
   the eight info marks on the dashboard's parts sit inside it. The first Escape
   on a focused mark is the mark's — it closes the caption — and must not also be
   the shell's; the next one, with nothing left to close, is. A host that counts
   is what tells those apart. *@

<div class="escape-host" data-testid="host" @onkeydown="OnHostKeyDown">
    <InfoHint AriaLabel="About Score" Text="Two scores." TriggerTestId="mark" />
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>Every key that reached the host, in order.</summary>
    public List<string> HostKeys { get; } = [];

    private void OnHostKeyDown(KeyboardEventArgs e) => HostKeys.Add(e.Key);
}
